.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt ZKEYS.TOML 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zkeys.toml
.Nd configuration file for zkeys
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file configures the
.Xr zkeys 8
client.
.Pp
This file is TOML-formatted and its main purpose is to define a table of keys
available for retrieval.
.Sh FORMAT
The following example shows a typical configuration file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
service_url = "https://zkeys.jmmv.dev/"
default_key_refresh_period = "5m"

[keys.sample]
id = "01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-4567890abcde"
remote_password = "foo"
local_secret = "baz"

[luks.root]
key = "sample"

[zfs."tank/sample"]
key = "sample"
.Ed
.Ss Security
The configuration file contains the remote passwords used to retrieve keys and
may contain a local portion of a secret.
Restrict read access to the file to the account that runs
.Nm zkeys .
.Ss Top-level settings
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Va default_key_refresh_period
Refresh period to use as fallback when teh service fails to provide a recommended
period for a key.
Durations are specified as a number followed by a unit, such as
.Dq 30s ,
.Dq 5m ,
or
.Dq 1h .
.Pp
Default:
5m.
.It Va service_url
URL of the zkeys service.
The URL must not contain a path.
.Pp
Default:
.Dq https://zkeys.jmmv.dev/
.El
.Ss Keys
Each key is declared in a
.Va keys . Ns Ar name
table, where
.Ar name
is the local name passed to the get-key and keep-alive commands or referenced
by the
.Va key
setting in a
.Va luks
or
.Va zfs
table.
Each table must contain the following settings:
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Va id
The UUID that identifies the key to the zkeys service.
.It Va remote_password
The password required to retrieve the key from the remote service.
.It Va local_secret
The local portion of the secret (not known by the service), prepended to the secret
returned by the service.
.El
.Ss LUKS volumes
Each LUKS volume is declared in a
.Va luks . Ns Ar volume
table, where
.Ar volume
is the mapper name of the volume.
Volume names must be non-empty single path components.
.Pp
Each table must contain the following setting:
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Va key
The name of a key declared in the
.Va keys
table.
Configuration loading fails if this key does not exist.
.El
.Ss ZFS datasets
Each ZFS dataset is declared in a
.Va zfs . Ns Ar dataset
table, where
.Ar dataset
is the dataset name and must be quoted if it contains a slash.
These entries map datasets to keys so that commands such as
.Cm zkeys zfs-change-key ,
.Cm zkeys zfs-create ,
.Cm zkeys zfs-load-key
or
.Cm zkeys zpool-create
can operate on them automatically.
.Pp
Each table must contain the following setting:
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Va key
The name of a key declared in the
.Va keys
table.
Configuration loading fails if this key does not exist.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zkeys 8
